# Copy to `.env.production` (gitignored) for a local production build
# (`npm run build`), or - the actual mechanism Vercel uses - set the same
# variable name/value as a Vercel Project Settings -> Environment Variables
# entry, scoped to the "Production" environment. Vite loads `.env.production`
# automatically whenever it builds in production mode (`vite build`, which is
# what Vercel's own build step runs), so no Vercel-specific build
# configuration is needed beyond that.
#
# Must be the deployed Render backend's exact base URL - https, no trailing
# slash. See frontend/.env.example for the equivalent local-dev variable
# (defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000) and frontend/src/api/client.ts for
# where this is read.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
